# AeroDash — sample environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (Vite picks it up automatically; `.env.local` is
# git-ignored so secrets / dev preferences never leak into the repo).
# All Vite-consumed variables MUST be prefixed `VITE_`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logger verbosity (frontend/src/shared/utils/logger.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both flags are OFF by default everywhere (dev, test, production builds) per
# issue #263 — DP-004 / CS-012 of the v0.3.0-alpha release audit. WARN and
# ERROR are always emitted; INFO is dev-only; DEBUG and TELEMETRY are opt-in.
# Accepted truthy values: `true`, `1`, `yes`, `on` (case-insensitive).

# Enable structured DEBUG output to `console.debug`. Useful when triaging
# behaviour locally; remember this overrides the production gate too.
# VITE_LOG_DEBUG=true

# Enable `telemetryTrace()`. WARNING: telemetry emits raw computation
# inputs/outputs (pilot-entered M&B / Performance / Fuel data) and BYPASSES
# the PII redactor by design — opting in is the operator's explicit
# acceptance that those values will land in `console.info`. Never enable in
# a production deployment.
# VITE_LOG_TELEMETRY=true
